tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lend-reaches-only-a-lent-parameter.hero:35:20: error[lend_kept]: `.cstr()` lends bytes to C for this call and no longer, and `s` of `keeps` is not declared to let them go — a C parameter without `lent` is assumed to keep what it is handed, and bytes kept past the call are read after the program has changed or freed them
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lend-reaches-only-a-lent-parameter.hero:36:19: error[lend_needs_a_header]: `.cstr()` lends a `str` to C for one call, and it may stand only as an argument of a function declared in an `extern` group — here the callee is this program's own, and no declaration of this program can say what becomes of the pointer
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lend-reaches-only-a-lent-parameter.hero:38:20: error[lend_kept]: `.ptr()` lends bytes to C for this call and no longer, and `p` of `parks` is not declared to let them go — a C parameter without `lent` is assumed to keep what it is handed, and bytes kept past the call are read after the program has changed or freed them
tests/golden/check/ffi-a-lend-reaches-only-a-lent-parameter.hero:39:19: error[field_lend_uncounted]: `.ptr()` lends a field's address to C with an extent this call states, and `p` of `bare` does not say which argument the extent is — so nothing can check the number against the field
